# Three spheres dropped from 2 m onto a hull ground. Their material restitution is
# 0, 0.5 and 0.9, which samples the post-solve restitution stage at three strengths.
# Reference: float box3d at 79fc559. The per-step traces include the impact step
# and the first bounce apex. Measured Linux max position/rotation/velocity
# (including angular): 0.00402832031, 0.00407409668, 0.00553894043.
# Header bounds are twice these maxima; awake counts agree exactly.
expect pos 0.00805664062 rot 0.00814819336 vel 0.01107788086 horizon 100 counts exact
world gravity 0 -10 0 dt 1 60 substeps 4 steps 100 restitutionIterations 2
body static position 0 -0.5 0 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
shape 0 box 10 0.5 10 density 1 friction 0.5 restitution 0
body dynamic position -3 2 0 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0 flags nosleep
body dynamic position 0 2 0 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0 flags nosleep
body dynamic position 3 2 0 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0 flags nosleep
shape 1 sphere 0.5 density 1 friction 0.2 restitution 0
shape 2 sphere 0.5 density 1 friction 0.2 restitution 0.5
shape 3 sphere 0.5 density 1 friction 0.2 restitution 0.9
